Doug Freyburger wrote:

> What do *you* mean by "good"?  At very least it needs to default
> to text-only, no HTML.  

Yes.

> It needs to quote using insert arrows 
> by default.  

Yes.

> It needs to put your cursor at the bottom by 
> default.  

Not at the bottom of the whole article, but under the first attribution
line so it's easy to go through the article trimming and replying as you
go. Putting the cursor at the bottom makes clueless people think they
don't have to trim, like putting the cursor at the top (above the
attribution) makes clueless people think top-posting is okay.

> It needs to nag you if you haven't trimmed. 

Only if it falls short on the previous one. People accustomed to trimming
don't need nagging; if they want to post fewer lines than they've quoted
it's usually because what they're saying needs all that context. Nagging
only encourages padding.

